# {{senseid|en|Q48103}} {{lb|en|physics}} The turning effect of a [[force]] applied to a [[rotational]] [[system]] at a [[distance]] from the [[axis]] of [[rotation]]. The [[moment]] is equal to the [[magnitude]] of the force multiplied by the [[perpendicular]] distance between its line of action and the axis of rotation.
